WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:02.010
- [Narrator] It's Election Day.

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:03.660
While it's unclear which races

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.910
Republicans and Democrats will win...

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.890
- It could be days, perhaps even longer

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.080
before we know the final midterm results.

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:11.250
- [Narrator] What is certain is that

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:12.810
this election looks different

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.610
for voters across the US.

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.220
- There are many laws in many states

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.800
that voters are gonna
be having to navigate

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.840
for the first time this year.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.460
- [Narrator] In the wake of
the contentious 2020 election,

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:25.830
(people screaming)

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:29.340
rules have changed and more
observers have been deployed.

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.380
Here's a look at how the
presidential election

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.680
made a lasting impact and
why some people are concerned

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.070
that the changes we see this
year from voting regulations

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:40.440
and voting methods to poll watchers,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.803
could affect voter turnout and
the future of our elections.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.750
At least 40 states have passed
laws in the last two years

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:52.110
that either tighten voting
rules or expand voting access

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:54.316
according to NYU's Brennan
Center For Justice,

00:00:54.316 --> 00:00:58.320
a public policy think-tank that
tracks election legislation.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.450
- If we're talking about
whether it's become harder

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:02.730
or easier to vote, and I
really think it depends

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:05.079
on where a voter happens to live.

00:01:05.079 --> 00:01:08.460
- [Narrator] Since 2020, 28
states have passed measures

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:10.800
that would make it easier
for eligible Americans

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.860
to register, stay, on the rolls, or vote.

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.870
In Vermont, all registered voters

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:18.270
will be mailed a ballot for
the November presidential

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:22.170
and midterm elections
under a law passed in 2021.

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:25.230
And in Kentucky, a new
law established three days

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:27.003
of early in-person voting.

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:29.550
- [Jasleen] Expansive
voting laws are recognition

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:32.010
by legislators that more access

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:34.440
means a more full, fair,

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.794
and engaged democracy.

00:01:36.794 --> 00:01:38.670
- [Narrator] 20 states have passed laws

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:41.190
that the Brennan Center
classifies as restrictive,

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:43.470
which can include measures
that shorten windows

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.690
to apply for a mail ballot,

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:48.810
limit the availability
of ballot dropboxes,

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:51.233
impose stricter signature requirements

00:01:51.233 --> 00:01:54.990
or impose stricter voter ID requirements.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:58.350
Among these are Arizona's HB2492 law,

00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:01.020
which established a proof
of citizenship requirement

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.850
for voter registration,

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:05.820
and Georgia's SB202, which requires voters

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:08.160
to provide an approved type of ID,

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.190
like a driver's license or
voter identification card

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:14.700
when requesting and
returning an absentee ballot.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.100
Republicans say the changes
were needed to restore

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.070
confidence among voters in
the integrity of elections,

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.650
while Democrats believe
the law is meant to depress

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:25.800
minority turnout, and that
former President Donald Trump

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:28.470
and his supporters corroded
faith in the process.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:29.453
- [Group] Give our taxes!

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.120
- [Narrator] No evidence of
widespread fraud has been found

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:36.270
in the 2020 election, but
the unsubstantiated claims

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:38.733
have motivated some
people to get involved.

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:41.790
While poll watching is a common feature,

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:44.040
where people monitor
ballot casting and counting

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.990
for possible rule violations,

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.600
there are concerns that
highly partisan volunteers

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.060
could try to intimidate voters this year.

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:53.220
- One of the features
of our election system

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.170
is this transparency,
the ability of people

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:56.550
to watch and observe,

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.740
but it also does create a vulnerability

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:00.420
if a bad actor gets in.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:03.090
- [Narrator] Trey Grayson oversaw
two presidential electionS

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:04.410
and two midterm elections

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.450
as Kentucky Secretary of State.

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:07.440
- We have to make sure

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.420
that the observers aren't
intimidating voters

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.760
or doing something that
they shouldn't be doing

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:13.860
during that observation process.

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.630
- [Narrator] The RNC says it has recruited

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:19.380
over 123,000 poll
workers and poll watchers

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.980
in primary, general, and
special elections this cycle.

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:26.310
The DNC said state level
democratic parties take the lead

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.290
on recruiting poll watchers.

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:31.050
- It all comes back to
balancing the transparency

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:33.990
of our system with not wanting
folks to be intimidated.

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:35.970
We don't want voters to feel

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.184
like somebody's watching or
will do something to them

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:41.010
and that causes them to not vote.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.530
- More than 43 million
ballots have been cast

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.690
as of November 7th, and there are signs

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:47.430
that this year's elections could meet

00:03:47.430 --> 00:03:50.820
or possibly exceed 2018's midterm turnout.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.950
It'll take until well after the election

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:55.410
when most or all mail-in
ballots have been counted

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:58.290
before we get a full picture
of voter participation.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:01.470
- We'll find out if that's
just a sign of people shifting

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:02.303
their voting preference

00:04:02.303 --> 00:04:04.353
or a sign of high overall turnout.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:07.050
- A recent Wall Street Journal poll

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:11.100
shows voter enthusiasm is
high with 81% of respondents

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.380
saying they definitely
will vote this year,

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:15.960
and 8% saying they already have.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.880
- I'm gonna be looking
for some of these new laws

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:19.530
that we're seeing in
states, how they work,

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.550
how they impact turnout

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:22.860
and also the the poll watcher issue.

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.570
And then finally, I wanna see the results

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.400
of some of these election
administrative races,

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.230
secretary of states and a few governors

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:29.460
that appoint secretaries

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.080
'cause that could have a tremendous impact

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.932
on the future of our elections.

00:04:32.932 --> 00:04:35.599
(gentle music)

